# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets — security headers (applied at the assets
# layer, which serves static files DIRECTLY and bypasses the worker's
# harden() — round-22 finding: the landing/privacy/terms pages shipped with
# ZERO security headers because harden() only runs for worker-handled routes).
# CSP matches worker.js's harden() exactly (inline script/style allowed for
# the single-page bundle; everything else locked to 'self').
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://monitor.toolfront.dev http://localhost:8787; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Link: </sitemap.xml>; rel="sitemap", </openapi.json>; rel="service-desc"

# Markdown charset: browsers without a charset declaration may decode the
# UTF-8 em-dashes/quotes in SKILL.md files as the OS locale (GBK on zh-CN
# systems) and show mojibake. Pin the encoding at the source.
#
# Note: the canonical /.well-known/agent-skills/* URLs are re-served by the
# worker (public/.well-known only holds security.txt), so _headers rules on
# that path never fire — the rule must target the /agent-skills/* storage
# path, which both the direct URL and the worker's ASSETS fetch pass through.
/agent-skills/*
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8
